WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.868
-Our next guest
is a talented actress

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:04.837
you know from the hit show
"The Summer I Turned Pretty."

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:07.206 line:0%
She's making her Broadway debut
in "Hadestown,"

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.075 line:0%
February 9th through March 17th.

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.610 line:0%
Please welcome to the show
Lola Tung, everybody.

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:14.046
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:17.049
[ Mid-tempo music plays ]

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:22.355
♪♪

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:25.058
♪♪

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.859
-Welcome to the show, Lola!
-[ Chuckles ]

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.794
Thank you.
Thanks for having me.

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:30.196
-This is your
"Late Night" debut.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:31.864
We're so honored
to be sharing it with you.

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:33.065
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:35.468
Wow. Yeah.
I'm thrilled to be here.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.936
-So,
"The Summer I Turned Pretty" --

00:00:38.003 --> 00:00:39.806
a massively popular show.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.641
Congratulations on its success.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:45.311
Also, your first acting credit.
That seems very surreal to me.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.414
I can only imagine
how it feels to you.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.950
-Yeah, I mean, it's wild,
and I can't even believe it.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:53.053
But, I mean, you know,
I did my fair share

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.054
of high school
and middle school theater.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:58.525
So, you know, it's been
a long road, but, yeah.

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:02.028
-What was your biggest role
in middle school?

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:04.797
-Um, okay.
I had a -- I was the Tin Man

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:06.098
in "The Wizard of Oz."
That's my first one.

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:08.501
-That's huge. Yeah.
How -- Looking back,

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.570
do you feel like
the costume was well made?

00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:13.639
-Oh, I mean, I think I,
like, thrifted the jacket,

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.308
and then I got some
silver rain boots.

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:17.343
-Gotcha. But it was enough.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.544
You felt like
you could act in it.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:19.778
-Oh, absolutely.
-Okay, good, good, good.

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:21.180
-Best ones are homemade.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:22.348
-I like that I thought
someone else would make it.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:23.950
I forgot,
middle school productions,

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:26.585
you literally came home and
you're like, "I got good news.

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:28.487
You're making me a costume."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:30.456
-Yeah, my mom was --
My mom was very supportive.

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.291
-Alright, that's good.
And then what about high school?

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:36.829
-Um, high school was, uh --
I didn't do as many shows.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.898
It was more like classes
and scenes.

00:01:38.964 --> 00:01:41.600
And I was studying drama
in high school, so, um...

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:45.438
I was, uh, Apostle Number 9
in "Jesus Christ Superstar."

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:46.873
-Alright!
-That was a good one.

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:49.542
That's my favorite of
the apostles in that show.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.110
-Thank you.
Yeah, it was a big one.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:54.680
-And you, uh -- you were then
at Carnegie Mellon in Pittsburgh

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.249
when you got cast in this,

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:59.919
and you were also going
to acting school in college

00:01:59.985 --> 00:02:01.821
during the pandemic.
So that meant masks,

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.589
which I'm wondering
what it was like,

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:06.793
being a student
doing acting with scene mates,

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:10.129
and you were all in masks.
-Yeah, I mean,

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:13.366
half of it was, like,
a lot of eye-contact work,

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:15.468
which is super fun.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:18.705
And then we did scenes
on Zoom.

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:21.273
So I was in -- at home
in my living room,

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:24.377
and my sister was on her online
classes in the other room,

00:02:24.443 --> 00:02:27.714
and I was, like, screaming
into the computer screen

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.882
at my -- at my classmates.
So that was...

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:32.251
-It's funny, I feel
like the pandemic was hard

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.620
for anybody who was studying,
but I do feel for your sister,

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.155
'cause I would imagine
the hardest is

00:02:36.221 --> 00:02:40.126
when your a family member
is a Zoom acting class.

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:42.161
-Oh, yeah.
Yeah, yeah, yeah, for sure.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.696
-Full emoting.
-Yeah.

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:47.934
-So, this show, again,
so popular, so fast.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.569
When did you start noticing

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:51.470
that it was a show
people were watching?

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:53.272
When did people
start approaching you?

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.707
-I mean, um, yeah --
Well, I mean,

00:02:55.774 --> 00:02:57.776
a couple days
after the show came out,

00:02:57.843 --> 00:03:00.880
I went to a Yankee game
with a couple of my castmates.

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:02.348
I'm a Mets fan, I'm not...
-Okay, gotcha.

00:03:02.414 --> 00:03:03.582
-Putting that out there.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:06.152
Um, but, um,
we went to the game,

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:09.622
and I remember, like,
just being stared at

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:12.258
a lot more than normal.
Like, nobody --

00:03:12.324 --> 00:03:13.693
I mean, I never --
You know what I mean?

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:14.928
-Right,
-You know what I mean.

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:17.296
And then, like,
seeing pictures on the Internet

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:20.332
that I didn't know were taken
from afar of, you know --

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:23.336
of just all of us hanging out.
And I was like, "Oh, man,

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:26.939
this is -- this is
a drawing attention, I guess.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:29.709
But I'm so happy
that the people love it."

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:31.377
-I would imagine,
when you first saw the part,

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.579
when you first read the script,
it must have felt like,

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:36.048
"Oh, this is such a cool part,
such a cool show."

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:38.084
You must have been
so excited

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.419
when you found out
you got it.

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:41.621
-Yeah, I totally was.
And I mean, I wasn't --

00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:43.589
I was in school
and kind of just

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.792
was like, "This is my path."

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:49.128
So it was cool to just have
a little, um --

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:50.729
be a little spontaneous
and have this --

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:53.399
this really amazing curveball
thrown my way.

00:03:53.465 --> 00:03:55.201
-You had a very
baller celebration

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:57.070
when you found out
you got this.

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.403
-Yes.
-What did you do?

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:00.072
Tell everybody,
because it is exactly

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:01.607
what I would do
if I got a huge part.

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:04.443
-Okay, I'm glad. I mean,
it's the only thing to do.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.913
My roommates came home,
and we all made dinner

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.849
and watched "Zootopia."
-Yeah.

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:11.184
-That was...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.586
Yeah. Shout-out to them.
-That's how you do it.

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:15.688
-Yeah.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:18.691
It was awesome.
-You probably called them

00:04:18.757 --> 00:04:20.226
and are like, "You guys
want to watch 'Zootopia'?"

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:22.195
And they were like,
"What happened?

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:24.797
What are we celebrating?"
-We do it for all events.

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:26.799
All -- All exciting moments.

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:29.469
-So, you -- you went viral
on TikTok

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:32.204
with an answer to a question,
which I, watching it,

00:04:32.271 --> 00:04:34.540
it's just you
authentically reacting.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.843
And were you surprised
that this became something

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:39.945
that then had,
I guess, an online moment?

00:04:40.012 --> 00:04:41.547
-Absolutely.
I mean, I feel like

00:04:41.613 --> 00:04:44.283
you can't ever
really predict what goes viral.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.652
And I was just excited
about -- about a question.

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:48.354
-You were excited
about a question.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:50.390
First, I'm gonna show everybody,
in case they haven't seen it.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.391
Here's your reaction
to a question

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:54.327
that everybody was very taken
with your reaction.

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:56.295
-Yes.

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.764
[ Gasps ] Oh, my goodness,
I love this question!

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.633
Um, I think...

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.302
[ Laughter ]
-Right.

00:05:03.368 --> 00:05:05.204
I will say, I watched that,
and I'm like,

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:07.840
"Oh, that is very endearing."
-[ Laughs ] Thank you.

00:05:07.906 --> 00:05:09.575
-It's really fun.
Also, by the way,

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:11.843
I've done this show
almost 1,500 times.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.379
I've never asked a guest
a question

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:15.448
where they've reacted that way.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.683
I really feel like
I have to up my question game.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.285
-It was a question
about Taylor Swift music.

00:05:20.352 --> 00:05:23.155
So, you know, I mean,
I was very enthusiastic, but...

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:25.858
-But then other people --
Olivia Rodrigo,

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:27.860
Scarlett Johansson,
among others --

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:30.262
have then basically
used it to lip-synch.

00:05:30.329 --> 00:05:33.232
Let's take a couple
of looks at those.

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:36.769
-[ Gasps ] Oh, my goodness,
I love this question!

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:39.905
Um, I think...
-[ Gasps ] Oh, my goodness,

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:43.075
I love this question!
Um, I think...

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:44.744
[ Laughter ]
-So...

00:05:44.811 --> 00:05:46.578
what was it like
when you first started seeing

00:05:46.645 --> 00:05:48.614
that other people
were using your answer?

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:50.082
-I was like,
"Oh, this is so cute."

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:52.785
And then it's, like,
kinda weird to hear your voice

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:55.921
coming out of
Scarlett Johansson's mouth.

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:58.424
But super cool, so thanks.
Thanks, you guys.

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:00.059
[ Laughter ]
-Do you now,

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:01.894
when you get asked questions,
do you feel,

00:06:01.961 --> 00:06:04.063
like, a real pressure
to have a reaction to it?

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.031
-Well, I wasn't,
but maybe now I do.

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:07.699
I'm like, "Oh."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.766 --> 00:06:09.301
-I don't want to
put you in your head.

00:06:09.368 --> 00:06:11.770
but this next question I'm gonna
ask is really [bleep] good.

00:06:11.837 --> 00:06:14.439
Um, do you want to have
anything prepared?

00:06:14.506 --> 00:06:16.776
It's really good. No.
So, we mentioned

00:06:16.843 --> 00:06:20.245
your middle school and
high school stage work.

00:06:20.312 --> 00:06:23.249
And now you're gonna do
"Hadestown" on Broadway.

00:06:23.316 --> 00:06:25.451
How does it feel
to return to stage?

00:06:25.518 --> 00:06:27.419
-It's, like,
the best feeling ever.

00:06:27.486 --> 00:06:29.455
I mean, it's, you know,
where I fell in love

00:06:29.521 --> 00:06:32.658
with acting and all that,
so it's -- I'm so excited.

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:35.528
-And so what process are you --
obviously, the show

00:06:35.595 --> 00:06:36.929
is up and running right now.

00:06:36.996 --> 00:06:38.497
So, what is the process
for someone like you,

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:40.666
who's stepping into the role?
Like, what are rehearsals?

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.868
-Um, it's, uh,
working with, like,

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:44.269
the dance captain
and the directors

00:06:44.336 --> 00:06:46.038
and a bunch
of the amazing swings.

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:49.642
And then I'm also
in rehearsal with Ani DiFranco,

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:52.311
who's stepping into Persephone
really soon --

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:53.679
one of the other roles
in the show.

00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:55.414
And that's been, like,
the coolest thing ever,

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:56.848
'cause she's awesome.

00:06:56.915 --> 00:06:59.151
And, um,
I'm just having a blast.

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:01.586
I mean, it's like
we've learned the show

00:07:01.653 --> 00:07:02.921
and we've done it
a couple times,

00:07:02.988 --> 00:07:05.357
so it's starting
to feel -- feel real.

00:07:05.424 --> 00:07:07.726
-And when you now
have access, obviously,

00:07:07.793 --> 00:07:11.730
to maybe a slightly better,
if not free, discounted tickets,

00:07:11.797 --> 00:07:13.732
are family and friends
coming out of the --

00:07:13.799 --> 00:07:15.734
Are they like,
"Don't forget me, Lola.

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:18.337
I watched 'Zootopia' with you.
You owe me."

00:07:18.404 --> 00:07:21.574
-[ Laughs ]
It's funny 'cause I, you know,

00:07:21.641 --> 00:07:23.475
I mean, I think most of
my friends and family

00:07:23.542 --> 00:07:25.878
were very quick to jump
to buy tickets

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:28.980
when the announcement came out,
so I'm grateful for that.

00:07:29.047 --> 00:07:30.749
A lot of people
are coming to see it.

00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:32.785
Some of my college friends.

00:07:32.851 --> 00:07:35.654
So, yeah, I'm super excited
that they can be there.

00:07:35.721 --> 00:07:36.956
-It's really wonderful.

00:07:37.023 --> 00:07:39.058
Congratulations on all
your success, the show,

00:07:39.124 --> 00:07:41.694
and I'm looking forward
to you in "Hadestown."

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:43.829
Break a leg out there.
-Thank you so much.

00:07:43.895 --> 00:07:47.099
-Lola Tung, everybody.
You can see her in "Hadestown"

00:07:47.165 --> 00:07:50.135
on Broadway,
February 9th through March 17th.

00:07:50.202 --> 00:07:52.138
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

